@@ -42,6 +42,19 @@ app.use(async (event) => {
 >
 > The examples below use a hardcoded value so they stay readable, but in a real app load a randomly generated secret of at least 32 characters from an environment variable such as `process.env.SESSION_PASSWORD`, and never commit it to source control. A guessable passphrase (even one ≥32 characters) is not safe.
 
+### Rotating the password
+
+To change `password` without signing users out, move the old value to `extraUnsealPasswords` and set the new one as `password`. Sessions sealed with an extra password still open, and each one is resealed with `password` the next time it is read from its cookie. Remove the extra once old cookies have rotated.
+
+```js
+const session = await useSession(event, {
+  password: process.env.SESSION_PASSWORD_NEW, // seals every new cookie
+  extraUnsealPasswords: [process.env.SESSION_PASSWORD_OLD], // only opens old cookies
+});
+```
+
+Extra passwords must meet the same minimum length as `password`. Keep the list short: each extra password tried on a cookie costs one more PBKDF2 derivation.
+
 This will initialize a session and return an header `Set-Cookie` with a cookie named `h3` and an encrypted content.
 
 If the request contains a cookie named `h3` or a header named `x-h3-session`, the session will be initialized with the content of the cookie or the header.
